Call site f.Write(trailer) on an *os.File, the first operand of Seal's errors.Join and
the oracle for seal_join_silent_truncation. Expected: os.ErrInvalid (nil file),
io.ErrShortWrite (File.Write), and the poll/syscall write errors, among them
io.ErrUnexpectedEOF, poll.ErrDeadlineExceeded, poll.ErrNotPollable and the opaque
"waiting for unsupported file type", under *fs.PathError.Unwrap, with os.ErrClosed
replacing poll.ErrFileClosing there. No errors.Join link (the Target is the operand).
The unwrapped copies of the poll/syscall values are the accepted over-approximation of
(*os.File).wrapErr described in the README ("if err == nil || err == io.EOF { return
err }" is a merge without phi, plan P07).
-- args --
source/source.go:@sealwrite
